Subject: Mark pizlonatedFIP<sig>_* function implementations hidden to prevent RTLD_GLOBAL interposition
Upstream-Base: llvmorg-23.1.6 (5b10d2d74929eae78912771222c9855af97496f4)
Fil-C-Head: e7b7f1e8969e24411b3d588bb9a043e5676f854d (branch deluge)

FilPizlonator emits each function's local FunctionObject (pizlonatedFO_<name>)
with a data pointer referencing the function implementation symbol
pizlonatedFIP<sig>_<name>. Previously, pizlonatedFIP<sig>_<name> inherited
F->getVisibility() (STV_DEFAULT), making that data relocation preemptible in
shared libraries.

When two shared libraries export a function with the same name and signature
(such as plugin entrypoints like PHP's get_module, Apache modules, PAM, or NSS)
and are loaded with RTLD_GLOBAL on a libc without RTLD_DEEPBIND (such as musl),
dynamic relocation interposes the first library's pizlonatedFIP<sig>_<name>
into the second library's pizlonatedFO_<name>. Consequently,
dlsym(handle2, "get_module") invokes library 1's implementation instead of
library 2's. The same interposition breaks dlsym(RTLD_NEXT, ...).

Keep pizlonatedFIP<sig>_<name> STV_HIDDEN (whenever it has non-local linkage,
after PutImplIntoComdat) so each DSO's pizlonatedFO_<name> resolves locally via
a relative relocation. Cross-DSO fast calls and symbol interposition continue
to use the exported pizlonatedFI<sig>_<name> GlobalAlias and pizlonated_<name>
getter, which retain F->getVisibility().

---
diff --git a/llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/FilPizlonator.cpp b/llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/FilPizlonator.cpp
index 32adbb8..93bece6 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/FilPizlonator.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Transforms/Instrumentation/FilPizlonator.cpp
@@ -16862,13 +16862,18 @@ public:
           ImplFuncTy, Linkage, F->getAddressSpace(),
           buf.str(), &M);
         FunctionToHiddenFunction[F] = NewF;
-        if (!UsesCallee) {
-          NewF->setVisibility(F->getVisibility());
+        if (!UsesCallee)
           FunctionToSignature[F] = Signature;
-        }
         NewF->setSubprogram(F->getSubprogram());
 
         PutImplIntoComdat(F, NewF);
+        // Keep pizlonatedFIP<sig>_* hidden so each DSO's local pizlonatedFO_*
+        // function object binds to its own implementation via a relative
+        // relocation instead of being interposed across RTLD_GLOBAL DSOs
+        // (e.g. plugin entrypoints like PHP's get_module or dlsym(RTLD_NEXT)).
+        // External callers still resolve the exported pizlonatedFI<sig>_* alias.
+        if (!NewF->hasLocalLinkage())
+          NewF->setVisibility(GlobalValue::HiddenVisibility);
 
         if (F->getLinkage() == GlobalValue::ExternalLinkage && !UsesCallee) {
           std::ostringstream buf;
